# Cloudflare Workers static-asset headers.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — two regressions the Vercel -> Cloudflare cutover
# introduced, both measured on prod, both invisible (nothing errors):
#
#  1. CACHING. Every file under /_next/static/ came back as
#     `cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` — Cloudflare's DEFAULT
#     for Workers static assets. vercel.json used to serve these (and the images
#     and fonts) with a one-year immutable policy. The effect of the default: a
#     returning visitor re-validates EVERY chunk, font and image on EVERY page
#     load. The edge answers 304 fast, but on Moroccan mobile data that is still
#     a round-trip per asset before the page can run.
#
#  2. SECURITY HEADERS. next.config.ts's headers() only decorates responses that
#     go THROUGH the worker. Static assets are served directly by the ASSETS
#     binding and bypass it entirely, so they lost `nosniff` and HSTS. Defence in
#     depth, but free to restore here.
#
# CACHE POLICY IS DELIBERATELY SPLIT BY WHETHER THE FILENAME IS CONTENT-HASHED:
#   • /_next/static/*  -> immutable, 1 year. SAFE: Next puts a content hash in
#     every filename (webpack-0a1ca1996446a3be.js), so a new build = a new URL
#     and a cached copy can never be stale. Same policy Vercel used.
#   • everything else  -> 1 day. These filenames are STABLE (favicon.png, the
#     TTFs, pdfjs wasm/cmaps/standard_fonts, logos), so `immutable` would pin a
#     stale copy in browsers for a year after a logo swap or a pdfjs-dist
#     upgrade. CLAUDE.md warns the pdfjs assets auto-resync on postinstall
#     precisely so they can't go stale — a 1-year pin would defeat that. One day
#     removes essentially all the repeat-visit cost while keeping updates same-day.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload

# Content-hashed by Next — a new build always produces a new filename.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Stable filenames: cache hard, but let a new version through within a day.
/pdfjs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/logos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/avatars/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/embedpdf/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/mediapipe/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/favicon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Employer landing pages (/pflege, built by scripts/build-pflege.mjs). Static files,
# so next.config.ts headers never reach them. Everything they need is self-hosted
# under /pflege/assets, so the policy can be strict: nothing loads from elsewhere
# except the Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon the edge auto-injects (script + /cdn-cgi/rum).
# borivon.com/ and /plattform are static files too (scripts/build-pflege.mjs).
/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
/index.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
/fahrplan
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
/fahrplan.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
/plattform
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
/plattform.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
/pflege/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
/pflege/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
